<title>POLAND: Polish insurer Polisa revises down '96 net plan.</title>
<headline>Polish insurer Polisa revises down '96 net plan.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish insurance company TUR Polisa SA revised down its 1996 net profit forecast to 3.7 million zlotys from 12 million forecasted in its issue prospectus last year, the company's president said.</p>
<p>Stanislaw Gutek told reporters the lower profit was due to high level of damages ratio in the whole insurance sector in early 1996 and the company's public offering offering in late 1995.</p>
<p>He said he expected its net profit to grow to five million zlotys in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Malgorzata Rzepka +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
